  "name": "Cardamom Rice Pudding",
  "description": "Creamy stovetop rice pudding scented with cardamom and orange.",
  "ingredients": "1/2 cup short-grain rice\n4 cups whole milk\n1/3 cup sugar\n6 cardamom pods, lightly crushed\n1 orange, zested\n\nPinch of salt",
  "directions": "1. Rinse the rice and put it in a heavy pan with the milk, sugar, cardamom and salt.\n2. Simmer gently for 35 minutes, stirring often, until thick and creamy.\n3. Fish out the cardamom pods and stir in the orange zest.",
  "notes": "Thickens as it cools; loosen with a splash of milk.",
  "servings": "4 servings",
